        "orario": "21:34",
        "timestamp": 1776368064,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. French billionaire Bolloré sparks turmoil at Grasset as 115 authors leave publishing house France Issued on: 16/04/2026 - 21:34 French conservative billionaire Vincent Bolloré came under attack from dozens of authors on Thursday at one of his flagship publishing brands, as he continues to reshape the country's media landscape. More than 100 authors at the Grasset imprint, home to some of the biggest names in French literature, said they would leave the publishing house after the surprise departure of its long-time CEO. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports. Debate on French bill outlawing ‘new forms of anti-Semitism' pushed back 16/04/2026 France Antisemitism and apology for terrorism 'already illegal in France': Is Yadan Law 'really necessary?' 16/04/2026 France French MPs introduce bill to remove statute of limitations for crimes against children 15/04/2026 France French court jails Lafarge former CEO for funding IS in Syria 13/04/2026 France Celine Dion to perform 16 concerts in Paris 12/04/2026 France Paris marathon marks its 50th year 11/04/2026 Sport France: French former prisoners in Iran describe detention conditions 08/04/2026 France One Health Summit begins in Lyon, France: How to prevent health risks ? 05/04/2026 France New Paris mayor Emmanuel Grégoire vows end to sexual violence in schools 04/04/2026 France"
